  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1100 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nThe big storm system will be moving off to our northeast Friday\nmorning, though some residual light precip is possible across the\nPlateau. Temperatures are forecast to rise into the 40s Friday\nmorning, so any wet/slushy accumulation should melt quickly,\nespecially with arrival of sunshine with clearing skies.\n\nIt appears we'll experience a brief warm-up for Saturday and\nSunday (highs in the 50s and 60s) with an increasing \nsouthwesterly breeze ahead of another shortwave trough. This \nsystem will bring another cold front and chance for light rain \nSunday into Sunday night.",
